# arena_wordptr.tkr — the §16 arena sub-crumb C fixture. `main.tks` bump-allocates a fresh
# NUL-terminated copy of "x" via `teko::mem::as_cstr`, bridges its opaque address to an `i64` word
# via `teko::sys::ptr_word`, recovers the pointer from that word via `teko::sys::word_ptr` — the
# inverse intrinsic this fixture exists to prove — and issues
# `teko::sys::syscall3(sys::SYS_WRITE, 1, teko::sys::ptr_word(back), 1)`, the raw x86_64 Linux
# `write(1, back, 1)` syscall, writing "x" to stdout through the RECOVERED pointer before exiting
# 0. The harness observes exit code 0 and stdout "x", proving `word_ptr` handed back a live,
# dereferenceable `ptr` equal to the original `as_cstr` buffer, not merely a type-checked opaque
# value.

Feature: arena_wordptr — word_ptr recovers a working ptr from an i64 word (inverse of ptr_word)

  Scenario: wordptr_roundtrip_prints_and_exits_zero — the recovered pointer writes "x" and exits 0
    When the program is built and run
    Then it exits 0
